 3. AI infrastructure demand surges 
 
 By Courtenay Brown 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data: U.S. Census Bureau; Note: Not adjusted for inflation; Chart: Courtenay Brown/Axios U.S. businesses kept investing heavily in equipment in September, extending a stretch of strong demand for manufactured goods largely fueled by the AI infrastructure boom.

 Zoom in: Demand for equipment associated with AI has surged at a pace not seen in recent decades.

 Orders for computers and related products, such as servers, storage devices and peripherals, surged 27% from a year earlier — including a nearly 4% increase in September alone. For a faster annual pace of growth, you'd have to go back nearly 30 years to January 1997. The bottom line: "The strong AI spending continues to drive business investment, and there are spillovers and strengthening [capital expenditures] outside of tech even amid higher borrowing rates and energy costs," Nationwide chief economist Kathy Bostjancic wrote in a note.

 
 
